# Design: Render reports and profile summaries (T037)

## Problem
Run reports and profiles are frozen JSON. Hosts and the future CLI
need readable terminal and Markdown views that stay honest about what
was measured, what was generated, and what authorizes nothing.

## Approach
One pure module, packages/measuretwice/src/render.ts, with two detail
levels per view. Summaries lead with check meaning, outcomes, the
aggregate, and the next action; details add rules, measurements,
identities, versions, counts, evidence references, and limitations.

## Key Trade-offs
- Explanations are generated at render time, not stored in the report.
  The frozen report shape of T034 stays untouched, and the text stays
  reproducible from recorded data alone.
- The renderer recomputes the decisive masses for display, but states
  one cutoff sentence only when the recorded masses support the
  recorded outcome. A record outside the decision table renders with
  the general sentence of its outcome, so the view never claims
  arithmetic the record does not support.
- The public Profile type gained the optional evidence and performance
  fields of contracts/v0/profile.schema.json. The fields were always in
  the artifact; the type now states them so profile detail can cite
  datasets, counts, and intervals without a cast.
- No performance number renders in one summary view, per the rule that
  no illustrative number may pose as a measured result.

## Gotchas
- The definition must hash to the hash the report names, or the render
  fails with definition_mismatch: check names are the definition's, so
  a wrong definition would misstate the meaning.
- The commit also repairs the pre-existing typecheck failure from T036
  in tests/repo/fixtures.test.ts (toContain does not take a message
  argument in the Vitest 5 typings; the note moved into expect).

